performance[quadratic]: `result` is copied on every loop step
 --> positive.jl:5:9
  |
5 |         result = vcat(result, part)
  |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ builds new `result` from old one
  |
  = why: each step copies all earlier pieces, so total work grows with square of length
  = fix: `append!` or `push!` into `result`, or collect pieces and join once (`reduce(vcat, pieces)`)   [manual]
  = docs: corset explain quadratic

performance[quadratic]: `rows` is copied on every loop step
  --> positive.jl:11:5
   |
11 |     rows = [rows; next_row()]
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ builds new `rows` from old one
   |
   = why: each step copies all earlier pieces, so total work grows with square of length
   = fix: `append!` or `push!` into `rows`, or collect pieces and join once (`reduce(vcat, pieces)`)   [manual]
   = docs: corset explain quadratic

performance[quadratic]: `count(==(name), names)` scans `names` on every step of loop over `names`
  --> positive.jl:15:8
   |
14 | for name in names
   |     ------------- loop over `names`
15 |     if count(==(name), names) > 1
   |        ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ linear search per element
   |
   = why: nested scan makes loop quadratic in length of `names`
   = confidence: possible
   = fix: build `Set(names)` or `Dict` once before loop   [manual]
   = docs: corset explain quadratic

